   "notes": "Headline model: the 1.3B ALiBi LM (25 layers, d=2048, 16 heads, FFN 8192) named in the abstract. It was trained on CC100+RoBERTa with L=512, 1024 and 2048; 1024 is the length given in the abstract. The WikiText-103 config is the Baevski & Auli model with sinusoidal embeddings replaced by ALiBi. For that config the paper says it ties the word embedding and softmax matrices, but this is not stated for the 1.3B model, so tied_embeddings is left not_stated. Its training length varies from 64 to 3072, so context_length is not_stated. The Books setting uses a 29K BPE vocab with tied embeddings. Left not_stated because the paper does not give them: norm type and placement, FFN activation, biases, vocab size, head_dim, and the attention scale. A footnote implies the standard sqrt(d_k) scaling is used but gives no value. The norm and activation ops are therefore omitted from block_ops, and the residual adds are the standard transformer assumption, not stated. The ALiBi bias is carried by positional=alibi and described in mechanisms_outside_ir, because the attention op has no bias attribute."
  },
